[...]
> Opinions? Criticisms? Other ideas?

Sounds good. If someone codes it well, IMO it could be the kind of thing 
the DevTeam might look at for a major release. Dragons are a little bland 
right now; making each one different enough to require individual handling 
could enhance the game nicely.

> Lung/Long Dragon: Instead of Orange (from East Asian Legends)
>  (no wings, can fly (no coding change))

If it has magical levitation, maybe its scales have some lightening effect? 
Uncontrolled levitation is no good; controlled possibly too powerful. 
Perhaps it could have some effect on carrying capacity? This might be too 
powerful if it multiplies the effectiveness of a BoH; perhaps reduce the 
weight of each item in the main inventory by a set amount, with a minimum 
of 1 weight unit?

> Wyvern: no claw attacks, add a sting attack,
> Instead of Green (Poison seems to fit the wyvern legend)

Poison makes sense, but is no threat to the average adventurer by the time 
they meet dragons. A paralysis sting attack and scales with an alternate 
source of free action perhaps? Sickness could be an alternative. Not sure 
of the scales should remain poison or resist sickness in that case. 
Sickness resistance would certainly make them more attractive. Eating the 
corpse should give poison resistance in any case, IMO.

> Guivre: instead of Yellow (or whatever), no limbs, can't fly. (add
> hugging?)

Having a dragon with a crush or grab attack is an excellent idea - by the 
time I meet dragons, I'm only worried about ';' with grab attacks; a single 
blessed genocide effectively removes this threat from the mid to late game 
(also see below re. genocide).

As black dragons are the only monsters with a disintegration attack, it 
would be best to give one of the dragons that ability.

I assume you'd be keeping DSM? I reckon you'd need to keep a DSM with magic 
resistance - IMO, MR is too important to be available only from one non-
artifact. Other than that, you could tailor the resistances to the dragon's 
ability. One possibility might be to give two "lesser" extrinsics to some 
DSMs; this could make them more viable as alternatives to MR/reflection. 
Lifesaving DSM could be quite amusing; you survive, but lose a load of AC! 
I would arrange the code to use other forms of lifesaving first, to make 
this viable as a backstop. Keeping colours for DSM could add flavour as it 
will tell you what colour the related dragon is.

If some dragons become tough enough for players to notice, it might be 
amusing to "genocide" DSM along with the dragon - i.e. if you genocide a 
type of dragon, the related DSM loses its magic ("Your scaly armor loses 
its magic and disintegrates" or somesuch). This would add a choice to the 
game - which DSM to wear and which dragons to genocide, or blessed genocide 
D and wear mithril? Making the "best" DSMs associated with the toughest 
dragons would make sense for this scheme.

So I guess I'm suggesting a tough MR "guivre" with a crush attack, and a 
silvery amphibious "leviathan" with a grab attack that's nearly as mean...

In case anyone thinks I'm advocating utter killer dragons, I'm not 
suggesting they should be Demogorgon, archon or even arch-lich tough, just 
sufficient to cause a pre-ascension-ready character to at least register 
which type they are before wading in...


